# Tutorials — how to use the system

## Content first (workflow playbook)

Tutorials teach **how to use the system**, not obvious chrome.

- Sections = important actions (create, fill required fields, work the record, convert, etc.)
- Do **not** devote chapters to view toggles, search boxes, paging, or other controls users already understand
- Mention list helpers only as a short “also useful” footnote when needed

## Where content lives

- **Seed markdown** (defaults): [`app/services/tutorial_seeds.py`](app/services/tutorial_seeds.py)
- **Admin overrides / custom steps**: `tutorial_sections` table via `/tutorials/{id}/content` and section CRUD APIs
- **Frontend registry**: metadata only (id, title, summary, category, access) — no JSX section bodies
- Admins edit **inline** on the tutorial detail page (markdown textarea + preview)

## Media

- Gate with `allows_media` on the merged section (seed or admin toggle)
- Upload category `tutorial-media`; Replace/Clear only when `allows_media` is true
- Never reuse one screenshot across unrelated sections
- Text-only chapters must not reserve an empty media column

## Layout

- Media section: two-column when asset or admin empty slot
- Text-only: single-column copy
- Guide TOC + chapter headings
